                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "After playing the first game, Defend the Highlands, I had to buy this immediately. This is one of games that enjoys being a game. The campaign is hilarious, the skirmish mode is really fun, and the characters are ridiculous (in a good way). I played this during the Early Access phase… which to their credit I did not realized until I began writing this review. The game is a solid play. I did not experience any technical issues. I did buy the game crazy cheap but the current $10 tag is appropriate. Compared to the first game this is way cleaned up. The battles, though still funny, are often very battle-like (i.e. your turnip shooter looks more like a machine gun than the last game which was clearly shooting turnips). I would actually enjoy seeing this developer make a Civil War, WWI, or WWI game. Or maybe a Defend the Highland from SPACE! Oh man that would be so awesome! Anyway it’s a fun little game that I would recommend if you want to mix up from your library a bit\n\n-------- Short Version Below ----- \n\nStory: Hilarious campaign. It is not a serious “change your life” kind of story. More or less its just about having a good time.\n\nReplay Ability: The game has a skirmish mode which allows you to replay. I played the skirmish mode more than the story. I just wanted to keep trying different tactics. The enemy is funny enough that you’ll run into a few ‘wtf moments.’ Like when a bunch of Nuns are being shot by Abraham Lincon or Samurai getting hit in the head with whiskey bottles.  \n\nGraphics: The graphics are perfect for the game. \n\nSound: The voice acting is great. The music is awesome.\n\nAchievements: The achievements were relevant to  the game play and did not force you to use multiplayer.",
